                        <div id="page-title">
                            SCP-5764
                        </div>
                    

                    

                    



                    <div id="page-content">
                        

<div style="text-align: right;"><div class="page-rate-widget-box"><span class="rate-points">rating:&nbsp;<span class="number prw54353">-13</span></span><span class="rateup btn btn-default"><a title="I like it" href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.modules.PageRateWidgetModule.listeners.rate(event, 1)">+</a></span><span class="ratedown btn btn-default"><a title="I don't like it" href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.modules.PageRateWidgetModule.listeners.rate(event, -1)">&#8211;</a></span><span class="cancel btn btn-default"><a title="Cancel my vote" href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.modules.PageRateWidgetModule.listeners.cancelVote(event)">x</a></span></div></div>
<h1 id="toc0"><span><strong>WARNING: USE OF SCP - 5764 ON OTHER SCPS AND ANY HUMAN BEING REGARDLESS OF CLASS IS STRICTLY BANNED BY THE ETHICS COMMITEE DUE TO THE ENTITY'S DEMANDS FOR ITS USE</strong></span></h1>
<p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5764</p>
<p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Safe</p>
<p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP 5764 is impossible to contain physically, instead, it was convinced by the foundation to stay at Site-43, in a standard cell. His presence is to be monitored constantly, as he roams the site's halls, passing through walls and occasionally slipping into any room imaginable, including another SCP's cell, these accidents only take mere moments to solve however, and no lasting negative effects on the staff or the scps has been detected. Conversing with SCP 5764 is to be put at a minimal level to avoid unnecessary distraction. A few incidents have occured as a result of staff attempting to coax the entity into doing various childish acts which result in the destruction of equipment or disruption of normal functions within a site for a certain amount of time. Any personnel caught attempting to coax the entity into creating an incident will be punished with expulsion or in the worst case scenario, termination.</p>
<p>However, his presence and conversations improve staff morale considerably, thus permission from the site director must be granted when wishing to talk to SCP - 5764 for an extended period of time and is to be lightly monitored. One person must be assigned to converse with the entity frequently to foster a familial bond and keep it psychologically locked to the Foundation. This person will rotate with the rest of the staff on a given site to form even more familial bonds. In the event of a possible incident involving SCP - 5764, a cognitohazard must be used to slow down the entity. The entity is also shown to have no activity during the night hours, specifically from 12:00 PM to 5 AM due to an anomalous effect that plagues the entity's mind.</p>
<p>Due to the restrictions placed on the elimination of other SCPs via SCP - 5764, SCP - 5764 instead is relegated to become a part of the Task Force in the event of a Containment Breach. The entity however will only help those it has formed a close bond with, thus, those who have been confirmed to be on friendly terms with the entity will be rotated throughout various sites in order to ensure the quickest possible response to a containment breach.</p>
<p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5764, nicknamed &quot;The Hyperborean&quot;, &quot;Heimdall&quot; or &quot;The Janitor&quot; by sentient SCPs it has managed to contain is a humanoid entity of uknown origin which was located in the town of Bugrino, Russian Federation after reports circulated around the internet over various russian sites about an angelic ghost wandering the town at certain points in the day. These reports were found by the SCP Foundation and were quickly investigated along with every mention of it on the internet being terminated.</p>
<p>Its appearance is that of a 7 foot tall pale white young male, blue eyes with white hair up to his shoulders, long beard and a thick moustache which covers the entirety of its upper lip. On its head it wears a helmet of Scandinavian origin with a small pair of metallic wings attached to the left and right side separately. 2 pairs of wings are present and are located at the center of the spine, however they are not properly connected and as such they are floating closely by, each of them are 14 feet in length. Its clothing consists of a large light grey cloak which cover its entire body save for the chest, stomach and frontal part of the legs. When asked to remove the cloak, its clothing consists of a large brown fur mantle draped across its shoulders, a chain mail coat, AKA maille Harbegion, black armored pants and shoes. SCP - 5764 is also incredibly muscular in appearance.</p>
<p>The physical properties of SCP - 5764 are unknown and only through the entity's explanation of his physical state can the foundation get an idea of its capabilities. It appears to be in a soul like state whereby it can pass through walls without any complications but when given a physical item, the entity can pick it up without it simply passing through its hand, additionally, SCP - 5764 is observed either walking or floating/flying. Direct contact with SCP - 5764 can only be achieved if the entity itself makes contact, or rather if it wants to make contact as it is intangible to outside attempts. Further testing and calculations of HUM levels determine that SCP - 5764 can change its physical state at will with no proven limitations. As a result, he is impervious to seemingly all physical damage. Additionally, no electrical activity from its brain nor body has been found. When an x ray scan was permitted by the entity itself, the resulting picture showed no body, only intense light vaguely resembling its shape, even if the room in question was dimly lit.<br />
The entity can lift up to 10 tons in weight, anything above will pass through its body in the process of lifting. Its maximum speed is calculated to be at 10,000&#160;m/s.</p>
<p>However, the SCP's most powerful ability is the ability to send everything its &quot;soul&quot; touches to a &quot;nil state&quot; for an infinite amount of time, even the very concept is set to nil and cannot be replicated again, having only some similarities to the object in question still renders replication useless. The &quot;nil state&quot; is, as the entity puts it, the core baseline of existence and nothing more, the state in which the being is in infinite oblivion, without thought or action.</p>
<p>Testing of SCP - 5764 with SCP 871, the replicating cake confirms this. An instance of SCP 871 was allowed to multiply and then multiply again. SCP 5764 was then tasked with erasing the third cake. When it did so, the cake turned into pure concentrated light, about 1000 lumens bright at its original position before imploding and completely vanishing. After this took place, the cell was thoroughly scanned with lasers for any electrical or atomic presence of the object in question, but, absolutely nothing was found. 24 hours later, the second cake didn't multiply at all. It was then isolated and kept for a further 3 days, but still, nothing. The first cake however wasn't affected and kept multiplying. Thus, it is concluded that only one &quot;nil state link&quot; is established.</p>
<p>The only limitation to this ability is that it cannot set already committed actions to 0, it can only prevent actions from occuring after the entity in question is set to 0. Further testing was accomplished with the test subject being a pregnant mother rat and its pups. SCP - 5764 was then instructed to set a single pup to 0. After the pup was sent to oblivion, the mother rat then tried to give birth 3 days later, however, as soon as the pups could exit the womb, they were set to nil.</p>
<p>These test subjects however were extremely small, so to confirm its ability, the entity was tasked with erasing a Boeing 747-8 Airplane outside on an abandoned air strip in an anonymous location. The same results occured, the airplane turned to light and imploded in an instant.</p>
<p>Conversations with SCP - 5764 are described as normal, warm, casual and lively. Possessing high social skills and charisma, there was no cognitohazard or anomalous influence detected. However, it has an average intelligence and has been described as impossibly stubborn and childish at times. While it shows absolutely no agression to staff or d class personnel, it has a less favorable opinion towards other SCPs. Furthermore, SCP - 5764's cooperation with foundation personnel is of particular note and it clearly shows when initiating dialogue with the entity. It has also been observed speaking all languages fluently, even those no longer in use. Additionally, its brain is capable of negating any and all cognitohazards by converting the energy generated by it and dispersing it throughout its body. Regardless of the effects, it will cause the entity to feel nauseous, reducing its physical speed by 90% and reaction time by 50%. However, if the state is prolonged enough, the entity will grow aggressive and attempt to wipe out the cognitohazard. An entire facility was almost lost when SCP (the bell) was used on SCP - 5764. It was prolonged for 30.2 minutes without the entity's knowledge and in the last few seconds the entity was ready to take a swing at a nearby wall before stopping when the cognitohazard was removed. It is also completely inactive from 12 PM to 5 AM due to an anomalous effect which put it in a paralyzed state and a state of agony.</p>
<p>However, a key aspect of its psyche is that it views the Foundation as its family and it feels fear at the prospect of completely leaving the facility. The only condition the Foundation has to complete is the continuous line of forming close bonds with the entity. This can be achieved through normal and extensive conversation with the entity, the average time to form a proper bond being around 1 month.</p>
<p><strong>Incident 5764-1:</strong> The only major incidence which has arisen regarding SCP 5764 is when the entity tried to perform martial art techniques on the power grid at Site 43 after Dr. ████ attempted to coax the SCP - 5764 into &quot;slam dunking the power&quot;. MTF agents then convinced the entity to not commit the action, though, it states that it regrets not trying it. A second, backup generator was then installed at Site 43 in order to prevent a blackout caused by SCP - 5764. Further attempts at coaxing SCP - 5764 is strictly forbidden and any personnel caught in the act will be punished with expulsion and amnestics or possible termination.</p>
<p><strong>Incident 5764-2:</strong> A second incident involving SCP - 5764 occured at Site 43 when SCP - 5764 flew to the control room and broadcasted a verbal message across the whole site which solely consisted of shouting racial slurs for the next 2 hours. Dr. ████ who coaxed the entity into commiting the act was caught conversing with it before the broadcast. Dr. ████ was then immediately fired for intentionally causing the hijacking of telecommunications. Luckily, Agents were dispatched and successfully managed to convince SCP - 5764 to stop the shouting.</p>
<p><strong>Incident 5764-3:</strong> A third incident involving SCP - 5764 occured when SCP - 5764 was tricked into pulling the hair off a female doctor because it thought it was a rope. About 30% of the hair she had was completely lost and her scalp was filled with deep cuts which left her in a state of nausea. It was tricked by the doctor's former husband due to a prolonged history of domestic abuse which the husband felt needed to take vengeance for. Doctor ████ and ████ were later both fired.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;INTERVIEW&nbsp;LOG&nbsp;I</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Log&nbsp;I</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> SCP-5764<br />
<strong>Interviewing:</strong> Dr. Jeffrey (humanoid anomaly psychologist)<br />
<strong>Forward:</strong> Interview was conducted at site 43<br />
<strong>Transcript:</strong></p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Hello, can you hear me?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Yes, clearly, may I know your name?</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: No, we have just escorted you here, so I’ll be the one asking questions</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Very well, continue on.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey,: I’ve been told MTFI agents have managed to… convince you… to come here? What is your particular reasoning for this decision?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Certainly they have and certainly you feel odd, I can understand. My reasoning is simple, for years I couldn’t leave this island, not of any perceived threat, but because of the immense fear and regret I feel to this very day. So this was a welcoming yet safe place to call home.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Fear and regret, of what?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Of myself.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Of yourself? Please elaborate.</p>
<p>SCP-5764: My regrets are for the actions I have committed in the past that horrify me to this day. And the fear, good doctor, is for what could have happened if I escaped the little island I formerly resided in.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: I see, what actions in your past caused you to think this way?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: A very simple event, possibly even trivial to you and everyone else here, but for me it felt like the highest pain I could experience. I don’t even know how I was born… All I remember before I could see was light, pure, pure, light and before long it dimmed and became clearer. I saw snow, I saw trees, I saw nature and suddenly vast amounts of knowledge poured into my mind that I went from a mute to speaking every tounge man conceived of. It all made me frightened, confused and dazed to the point where I fled into the woods. Exploring the vast frozen swamps, I eventually came across human settlement. Men, women and children in their daily lives, happy and lively, it made me happy too, for a time at least. The last year I remember seeing was 1895, written on the wall of a nearby house. When I approached the villagers, they were terrified of me, except, for a small girl which was standing close to me, she wasn’t …afraid but… <em>(Moves head downwards and sighs)</em></p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: But what?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: But… but… I never knew her real name, I never once thought of asking, I only nicknamed her Lilly… The times I spent with her were among the best experiences I had so far in what could be called my life… shielding her whenever I could, playing with her and so on and so forth. Yet… all of that ended one night when I visited her in her room, lying on the bed. She was suddenly woken up by my presence. Wasting not a heartbeat, she reached out her arms to hug me and I followed suit. I heard cry and wondered what was going on but I lost myself in the affection and soon I could hear no cries, only a door swinging open. I opened my eyes and saw her parents standing by.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: I see…</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Soon, her parents stared at me with a mix of shock, horror and a small dose of delight. They both kneeled down and the husband spoke first. He apparently thought I was a god and that his daughter was sent to a higher place named “Hyperborea”. The husband begged me to send him and his wife to this… place too and called me “The Hyperborean” while doing so. Thus the name stuck. Somehow my emotions consumed me… and I felt as if I lost control of my mind for but a moment and that moment was enough to send Lilly’s parents to the eternal zero, the nil state, like I did with her. I was horrified, shocked… scared. I flew past the walls into the wilderness at full speed. I only stopped when I was in the dirt and all I could see was black… <em>(Long sigh)</em> Doctor… I’m tired.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Wait, nil state? What is a nil state? Where are you – Fine, it will be enough for today.</p>
<p><strong>End Transcript</strong><br />
Closing Statement: SCP-5764 Will need time to mentally recover. So far, his willingness to cooperate and his immense potential to serve Foundation interests warrant a second transcript as soon as his mental stress subsides.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;INTERVIEW&nbsp;LOG&nbsp;II</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Log&nbsp;II</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> SCP-5764<br />
<strong>Interviewing:</strong> Dr. Friedrich (humanoid anomaly psychologist)<br />
<strong>Forward:</strong> Interview was conducted at site 43<br />
<strong>Transcript:</strong></p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Hello, how are you feeling currently?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Better, I do apologise for the unnecessary scene I caused previously.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: No matter that now, we have something more important, you said something about a nil state? The 0 as you say. What is this state you can send people, things or whatnot into?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: The 0 state is the core baseline for existence itself, I simply override their existence with everything my soul comes in contact with to nil, or set them to nil directly if it is infinite or abstract so violently that any action which attempts to bring it back is instantly overrided and sent back, over and over again until, well, forever. The concept of anything I set to nil is also void and nothing can be reproduced further. It would be as if overloading a carriage to the point where it collapses and cannot store more things.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: How do you know all of this, being stuck on a small island in the middle of nowhere?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Revelation, my good sir. At random, when I… <em>(Sigh)</em> buried… myself into the earth, I had vision after vision of my capabilities, revealed to me in terrifying speed, torturing my mind with realizations of what I committed, if I had to describe it, it would be as if you had to experience severe migraines for a hundred years, every second non stop, but also other things, of this world and of existence. I can’t remember it all, it seems as if everything was revealed to me yet my mind couldn’t contain it, couldn’t withstand infinite knowledge. But it also gave me insight into what I can do as a being, or soul, or, I don’t know. Who revealed to me these abilities? Well, I don’t know, possibly the ultimate entity of the universe itself, possibly just random visions, I couldn’t tell you. They were both painful and insightful but they stopped after a hundred years and I finally rose to see nature again, subsequently leading to my arrival at this facility.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: So, you can return absolutely everything to a nil state?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Yes, though not all, actions committed by me or by other entities I can’t set to nil… otherwise… well, Lilly would be alive. But any further action to escape the nil state is automatically set to 0 in an instant.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: I apologise for barging in with this question but, I must ask you, do you know what the SCP Foundation is, exactly?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: The SCP Foundation? Well, I’m in one of your facilities and from exploring it I saw many twisted creatures existing comfortably inside concrete walls. From what I can tell, you are here to protect mankind from these creatures?</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Yes, and as you have been so cooperative, the Foundation requests of you to exterminate certain undesirable scps when the time is right.</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Your request, I must decline for I have only showed devotion to the foundation and yet it to me has shown none.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Then how can we show devotion?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: A hundred thousand innocent people must be sacrificed for my services, after which I will do my duty to this foundation for a hundred days. Don’t use your own,</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Why? Did your time in the dirt restrict your abilities in any way?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: No, they didn’t, it is simply my moral creed which I follow absolutely. Lives for lives, my good fellow, but keep in mind, I will not hesitate to bring this entire foundation down if you dare kill a single individual who does not fit my criteria. And you may fool me once, twice, even ten times, in the end, I will find out and all of you will be set to nothing, monster or not.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: And what doesn’t fit your criteria?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Criminals, swindlers, bastards of the earth, you know the type. Only moral blood must be shed.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: But then isn’t that immoral of you to request such a thing?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Yes, but it is immoral for you too to put forward a request to destroy these monstrosities permanently. You are sending 100,000 people to a better place while I send these monstrosities to infinite oblivion. Lives for lives.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: I see, even though we don’t know where this better place is exactly, I’ll respect your decision but make one more request, to confirm your abilities and utility, I want you to do testing on a few objects and one animal, do you object?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: No, I don’t.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Lastly, does the name Heimdall or Heimdallr ring a bell?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Only that it means home and bold or renowned. And that someone named Velimir Dobroslav, a man I met when I came out of that torturous hibernation occasionally asked me if I was the god named “Heimdall” and if you want me to answer that, you’ll get the same response Velimir got: I do not know.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Excellent, well, this interview is at an end.</p>
<p><strong>End Transcript</strong><br />
Closing Statement: SCP-5764 Ability to set anything it makes contact with to a nil state at will confirms his utter utility to the foundation in preventing other scps from going rampant and endangering thousands of lives, however, its demand, of which it was unwilling to change or alter is a major hindrance. Requesting for further dialogue between the entity to know of its origin.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;INTERVIEW&nbsp;LOG&nbsp;III</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Log&nbsp;III</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> SCP-5764<br />
<strong>Interviewing:</strong> Dr. Friedrich (humanoid anomaly psychologist)<br />
<strong>Forward:</strong> Interview was conducted at site 43</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Hello, I hope it doesn’t disturb you that I am once again interviewing you.</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Not at all, good doctor. The more time passes by, the more I get acclimated to this environment. Oh and, I now know your name, Dr. Jeffrey.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: How did you exactly figure out my name?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: A bit of flying here, a bit of conversation there, you know. Either way doctor, I believe this isn’t why you came here, is it? You have no cause for worry, I won’t suddenly erase you or keep tabs on you while you sleep or torture you or what not. Let us simply continue.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Fine, let’s get to the point. In your previous interview, you went to some length about your origin. The part that interests me is the revelations part. What exactly did you see?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Many things, I don’t remember them all and I honestly wish I didn’t for when I thought they wouldn’t return, they do. At random intervals throughout the night, usually starting at around 12, a vision will come back to haunt me. This could be anything, at times its just random information about random people, if I recall correctly, I even remember how your grandmother died, doctor.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Right, wai-, hold on what? How do you know that?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: I don’t know myself. Perhaps I’m but a cog, a servant of a greater being who’s pouring knowledge into my head, perhaps I’m a fallen god, who’s just reawakened, and who’s memories and future knowledge are pouring into his head at a fast rate, I simply do not know. Sometimes I see fire and hear screaming in my visions, these are the visions which force even a being such as I, a tear or two. I do not choose to live the way that would plague me with monolithic worry, I have enough of it.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Right, well, I’m convinced that you yourself are not hiding anything.</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Indeed, do you have any more questions?</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Yes, I would like to know, why do you like humans so much?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Because they are beings other than me who have true free will and are not abominations made to crawl about and cause havoc. I always thought of myself as a human, until my century long slumber did I realise that I was something uknown, abstract yet horrifying, a fitting punishment for erasing humans.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Alright, but, what puzzles me is why can’t you just erase them? Wouldn’t it be far simpler and better?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Yes, it would but truth be told, there is a bit of an unusual thought inside my mind that these creatures, objects or places are all human souls stuck to whatever vessel they’re in, be it a simple object or a body or a place, I always imagine them as human souls twisted by the higher anomalies, the true scum of existence. I also know the price for acting up, I know the torment I felt all because I decided to erase an innocent family.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: But can’t you realize how much you would be he-</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Yes, yes, I would, I get that <em>(sigh)</em>, I get that, but you have to understand that the pain I felt for a hundred years would make any man hesitant to repeat the same mistake and I’m supposed to be a god for crying out loud! I felt a great, beating pain in my head, like I was continuously hit by sledgehammers for every second of a hundred years. My mind became a prison cell and my body, a dulled out chisel, no longer usable to cut the bars that would set me free. Sorry to have to describe it like an angsty teenager but I hope you understand now that nobody would risk a hundred years of torment just to eliminate a few foes.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: I see, well, what am I to you? Am I a good friend to you?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: A bit of a twist in the conversation, doctor but I’ll bite, perhaps you are, I mean I already shared my secrets and have known users though not through your consent, still, I feel as if we are forming a decent bond with one another.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: And if I was in danger, would you rescue me?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: I would rescue you from any entity.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: What about if someone close to you died? Would you be able to annihilate then?</p>
<p>SCP-5764: No, not even then, I would only make the entity suffer, engraving myself into its psyche until they shudder each time I walk by, I’d make them feel pain each time they glanced at me, without laying a single finger. But don’t worry though, you’ll live, doctor, I wouldn’t let these sick creations on you like that.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Thank you, that is comforting.</p>
<p>SCP-5764: A comfort to your mind, now you need a comfort to your stomach, just wait a minute.</p>
<p><em>(the entity proceeded to bring a caffeinated beverage into the containment room, 7 minutes later)</em></p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Why, uhh, thank you,</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Feeling a bit strange that an anomaly gave you a drink?</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Yeah, but, still, thank you</p>
<p><em>(Dr. Jeffrey proceeded to drink the beverage and finished it within a minute)</em></p>
<p>SCP-5764: Well, I hope you like it, I’ll be leaving now and oh, I just remembered, I put a very special type of milk inside your coffee, I heard it does wonders for your nutrition.</p>
<p>Dr. Jeffrey: Wait, did you</p>
<p>SCP-5764: Until next time, Jeff.</p>
<p><strong>End Transcript</strong><br />
Closing Statement: After the interview, Doctor Jeffrey was taken to the hospital wing and no anomalous/hazardous substance was detected. This will officially be the last interview conducted with the entity as all suspicions and speculations about it are confirmed.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;[O5&nbsp;CLEARANCE&nbsp;REQUIRED]&nbsp;INTERVIEW&nbsp;LOG&nbsp;WITH&nbsp;THE&nbsp;ETHICS&nbsp;COMMITTEE</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Log</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> Dr. ████<br />
<strong>Interviewing:</strong> Dr. ████<br />
<strong>Forward:</strong> Interview was conducted at Site ██<br />
<strong>Transcript:</strong></p>
<p>Dr. ████: Hello, how are you today?</p>
<p>Dr. ████: I’m doing well, and you?</p>
<p>Dr. ████: Good and a bit nervous, because of a certain topic I suspect you have a strong opinion of?</p>
<p>Dr. ████: I assume this is about the new SCP the Foundation tried to weaponise?</p>
<p>Dr. ████: Yes, it is.</p>
<p>Dr. ████: Alright, fine, state what you want.</p>
<p>Dr. ████: The O5 council wishes to request a repeal of the ban on the use of SCP - 5764 against other SCPs.</p>
<p>Dr. ████: Doctor, with all due respect, you do know why we banned the use of this entity, don’t you?</p>
<p>Dr. ████: I do, but it is the O5’s belief that this ban will create more bad than good, especially when the power to erase all the threats to mankind lies in a simple conversation.</p>
<p>Dr. ████: And I ask you, what will this conversation morph into? First it’ll eliminate all the undesirable SCPs after 100,000 innocent men, women and children are sacrificed and then what? Slaughter another 100,000 to keep the peace? Hound it until it brakes and sends us to eternal oblivion? No, this proposal is absurd.</p>
<p>Dr. ████: (sigh) You don’t understand, do you, doctor?</p>
<p>Dr. ████: Understand what?</p>
<p>Dr. ████: This entity is our best ally against anything, you know what that means? Saving billions and billions of lives, the universe and beyond by a mere uttering of a word. So what? You’re so hung up on the 100,000 that would perish but stop to consider everyone who would be saved. For crying out loud, this thing can set gods to zero in an instant!</p>
<p>Dr. ████: I’m well aware of the benefits it would bring to humanity, yet you forget that this Foundation is willing to sacrifice hundreds of children just to appease some random entity in the hopes of “learning about it”. No, the Ethics Committee is tired of permitting such acts in the name of safety. The risks are too big.</p>
<p>Dr. ████: Then, perhaps a full ban is not necessary?</p>
<p>Dr. ████: What are you suggesting, doctor?</p>
<p>Dr. ████: I’m suggesting that it can be used in different, less risky ways.</p>
<p>Dr. ████: How so?</p>
<p>Dr. ████: Instead of eliminating SCPs, it can contain them.</p>
<p>Dr. ████: Contain them? How? He doesn’t like being a slave, he said it himself.</p>
<p>Dr. ████: Well, the entity has already shown a great deal of care for those it forms a close bond with. These bonds can be, let’s say, used to our advantage. Not in the sense that people will be randomly thrown into danger, but rather, get staff to communicate with the entity as it showed no hostility towards it and thus is not a threat to the well-being of personnel, then rotate them between facilities and if a containment breach were to occur, the entity would respond instantaneously.</p>
<p>Dr. ████: This? This is its only use?</p>
<p>Dr. ████: No, there would be another, more important use. In the event of a world ending scenario, species ending scenario, apocalyptic scenario ect, the ban would have to be lifted and 100,000 people must be sacrificed to ensure the safety of our planet and possibly the universe itself.</p>
<p>Dr. ████: And what if it doesn’t even want to comply or what if he can’t even stop it?</p>
<p>Dr. ████: In that case, the only thing we can do is dance a merry irish jig before being annihilated. If it is inevitable that billions have to die, it’s better to at least try only killing a hundred thousand rather than sitting back and doing nothing out of a completely irrational fear.</p>
<p>Dr. ████: (pauses for a minute) This will have to be consulted with the Ethics Committee. I myself agree with this statement but others may not.</p>
<p>Dr. ████: Affirmative, thank you for taking part in this discussion.</p>
<p>(3 days later)</p>
<p>Dr. ████: Hello, Doctor 5764, has the ethics committee decided on what to do with SCP - 5764 ?</p>
<p>Dr. ████: Yes, we have decided that your proposal is satisfactory and its only two uses will be to prevent containment breaches and k class scenarios.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;[O5&nbsp;CLEARANCE&nbsp;REQUIRED]&nbsp;POST-DISCOVERY&nbsp;LOG</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Log</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> Velimir Dobroslav<br />
<strong>Interviewing:</strong> Agent ████<br />
<strong>Forward:</strong> Interview was conducted 200&#160;km away from Bugrino, Kolguyev Russia.<br />
<strong>Transcript:</strong></p>
<p>Agent ████: Hello, I hope you can understand me. (in Russian)</p>
<p>Velimir Dobroslav: Yes, even your accent is nearly perfect.</p>
<p>Agent ████: Good, I am sure you understand why I’m here, Mr. Velimir.</p>
<p>Velimir Dobroslav: I do, it’s because of the Hyperborean, isn’t it?</p>
<p>Agent ████: “The Hyperborean” is an interesting name you gave to the entity that wondered around your little village recently. Why did you name it so?</p>
<p>Velimir Dobroslav: Because he is a magnificent being that confirms my beliefs.</p>
<p>Agent ████: Alright, what beliefs?</p>
<p>Velimir Dobroslav: That he is a messenger, a guardian of Hyperborea, a mystical land beyond the snow of suffering. A land in which all ancestral or what you Abrahamic traitors call “pagan” faiths believe exists in their own way, now revealed to us after a millennia of suffering at the hands of the false Hebrew God.</p>
<p>Agent ████: And you believe this mystical continent exists on Earth?</p>
<p>Velimir Dobroslav: No, it is beyond space and time.</p>
<p>Agent ████: Alright, so did you speak with the entity?</p>
<p>Velimir Dobroslav: Yes, but it was for a time, he didn’t seem to know about his mission but not all messengers do.</p>
<p>Agent ████: Alright, but, which god does he resemble most to you?</p>
<p>Velimir Dobroslav: To be fair, he does resemble the norse god, Heimdallr, the one who is destined to blow the horn on the day of Ragnarök.</p>
<p>Agent ████: Alright, thank you for your cooperation.</p>
<p>Velimir Dobroslav: What? Where are you going? Don’t you dare think he’ll bend to you!</p>
<p>Agent ████: (hastily walks out)</p>
<p><strong>End Transcript</strong><br />
Closing Statement: After conversing with everyone else who reported SCP - 5764 no one had any strong theories on his existence, except for Velimir Dobroslav. SCP - 5764 must first be interviewed to see if the entity can reveal its true origin. The people who reported the entity’s existence will be given amnestics shortly.</p>
</div>
</div>
